{"seconds": 435.789, "paras": [{"n": 1, "start": 0.41, "end": 8.52, "text": "In Sunrise on the Reaping, a sixteen-year-old boy's name is ", "cut": 8.9}, {"n": 2, "start": 9.28, "end": 21.06, "text": "It's fiction. But fifty-seven years ago, America did somethi", "cut": 21.59}, {"n": 3, "start": 22.12, "end": 34.37, "text": "Sunrise on the Reaping is based on something real. And by th", "cut": 34.85}, {"n": 4, "start": 35.33, "end": 44.95, "text": "Welcome to the Fiction Files. I'm your Detective. Every stor", "cut": 45.78}, {"n": 5, "start": 46.61, "end": 59.5, "text": "First, the fiction. In Panem, every child aged twelve to eig", "cut": 59.93}, {"n": 6, "start": 60.36, "end": 71.57, "text": "In Sunrise on the Reaping, it's even worse. It's the fiftiet", "cut": 72.0}, {"n": 7, "start": 72.43, "end": 83.76, "text": "But here's the detail most people forget. The reaping isn't ", "cut": 84.19}, {"n": 8, "start": 84.62, "end": 88.84, "text": "So the poorest kids have the worst odds. Remember that. It's", "cut": 89.37}, {"n": 9, "start": 89.9, "end": 101.26, "text": "Suzanne Collins has said the idea came to her one night whil", "cut": 101.69}, {"n": 10, "start": 102.12, "end": 108.01, "text": "She's also said she loved the Greek myth of Theseus, where A", "cut": 108.44}, {"n": 11, "start": 108.87, "end": 112.23, "text": "That's the version everyone's heard. Here's the one nobody t", "cut": 112.86}, {"n": 12, "start": 113.49, "end": 127.26, "text": "It's 1969. America is deep in the Vietnam War, and the army ", "cut": 127.69}, {"n": 13, "start": 128.12, "end": 130.78, "text": "So the government tries something new. A lottery.", "cut": 131.26}, {"n": 14, "start": 131.74, "end": 144.55, "text": "On the evening of December the first, 1969, at the headquart", "cut": 144.98}, {"n": 15, "start": 145.41, "end": 150.89, "text": "It's for men born between 1944 and 1950. And it's broadcast ", "cut": 151.32}, {"n": 16, "start": 151.75, "end": 158.63, "text": "A congressman named Alexander Pirnie reaches in and pulls ou", "cut": 159.06}, {"n": 17, "start": 159.49, "end": 163.9, "text": "If you were born on September the fourteenth, you are now nu", "cut": 164.43}, {"n": 18, "start": 164.96, "end": 175.2, "text": "One by one, the dates come out and go up on a board. Across ", "cut": 175.63}, {"n": 19, "start": 176.06, "end": 180.39, "text": "In the end, every man whose birthday came out in the first o", "cut": 180.92}, {"n": 20, "start": 181.45, "end": 190.74, "text": "Now, pause the video for a second. Find your birthday on thi", "cut": 191.87}, {"n": 21, "start": 193.0, "end": 206.15, "text": "To be clear, Suzanne Collins has never said this lottery ins", "cut": 206.73}, {"n": 22, "start": 207.31, "end": 208.62, "text": "But that's not the strangest part.", "cut": 209.15}, {"n": 23, "start": 209.68, "end": 213.72, "text": "Remember how the reaping isn't fair? The 1969 lottery wasn't", "cut": 214.15}, {"n": 24, "start": 214.58, "end": 223.26, "text": "The capsules had been put into the container month by month,", "cut": 223.69}, {"n": 25, "start": 224.12, "end": 239.9, "text": "So if you were born late in the year, you were more likely t", "cut": 240.33}, {"n": 26, "start": 240.76, "end": 247.99, "text": "In Panem, being poor put your name in the bowl more times. I", "cut": 248.67}, {"n": 27, "start": 249.35, "end": 251.15, "text": "Now here's where this case gets personal.", "cut": 251.68}, {"n": 28, "start": 252.21, "end": 262.23, "text": "Suzanne Collins's father was an officer in the United States", "cut": 262.66}, {"n": 29, "start": 263.09, "end": 271.53, "text": "She later wrote a picture book about that year, called Year ", "cut": 271.96}, {"n": 30, "start": 272.39, "end": 286.48, "text": "Collins has said her father felt it was his job to make sure", "cut": 286.91}, {"n": 31, "start": 287.34, "end": 294.58, "text": "So the woman who wrote the most famous story about children ", "cut": 295.31}, {"n": 32, "start": 296.04, "end": 299.96, "text": "And there's one more piece of evidence. It's the key to Sunr", "cut": 300.39}, {"n": 33, "start": 300.82, "end": 311.67, "text": "When Collins announced the book, she said it was inspired by", "cut": 312.1}, {"n": 34, "start": 312.53, "end": 328.68, "text": "Hume's question was simple. Why do millions of people let a ", "cut": 329.11}, {"n": 35, "start": 329.54, "end": 341.59, "text": "Even the country's name is a clue. Panem comes from an old R", "cut": 342.17}, {"n": 36, "start": 342.75, "end": 345.47, "text": "Now look at what happened in America in the weeks before the", "cut": 345.9}, {"n": 37, "start": 346.33, "end": 355.46, "text": "On November the third, 1969, President Nixon went on televis", "cut": 355.89}, {"n": 38, "start": 356.32, "end": 363.539, "text": "Twelve days later, hundreds of thousands of people marched o", "cut": 363.969}, {"n": 39, "start": 364.399, "end": 367.439, "text": "Sixteen days after that, the lottery was drawn on live TV.", "cut": 368.119}, {"n": 40, "start": 368.799, "end": 380.599, "text": "The many, and the few. Some people stayed silent. Some peopl", "cut": 381.279}, {"n": 41, "start": 381.959, "end": 383.769, "text": "So, let's look at the evidence.", "cut": 384.199}, {"n": 42, "start": 384.629, "end": 405.959, "text": "A real government really did draw young people's birthdays f", "cut": 406.389}, {"n": 43, "start": 406.819, "end": 414.679, "text": "There's no real arena. No real tributes fighting to the deat", "cut": 415.259}, {"n": 44, "start": 415.839, "end": 419.979, "text": "So, how real is Sunrise on the Reaping? The evidence says\u2026 e", "cut": 420.759}, {"n": 45, "start": 421.539, "end": 434.439, "text": "Case closed. Don't forget to tell me your 1969 number in the", "cut": 435.789}], "words": [["in", 0.46, 1], ["sunrise", 0.62, 1], ["on", 1.06, 1], ["the", 1.23, 1], ["reaping", 1.44, 1], ["a", 2.32, 1], ["sixteen", 2.32, 1], ["year", 2.64, 1], ["old", 2.91, 1], ["boy's", 3.13, 1], ["name", 3.46, 1], ["is"